<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Twenty-second Dynasty of Egypt</h1><p class="st-meta">943 BCE – 720 BCE (approx.) · capital Bubastis</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Libyan pharaohs of Bubastis, founded by Sheshonq I, the biblical Shishak, whose realm gradually split into rival kingdoms.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shoshenq-i">Sheshonq I</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-chief-of-the-ma">Great Chief of the Ma</a> and descendant of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/meshwesh">Meshwesh</a> settlers at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bubastis">Bubastis</a>, succeeded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/twenty-first-dynasty-of-egypt">Twenty-first Dynasty of Egypt</a> around 943 BCE. He reunited the country by appointing his sons to key posts, including the high priesthood of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amun">Amun</a> at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shoshenq-i">Sheshonq I</a> campaigned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a> around 925 BCE, recorded on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bubastite-portal">Bubastite Portal</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnak">Karnak</a> and in the Bible as the attack of Shishak on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osorkon-i">Osorkon I</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osorkon-ii">Osorkon II</a> endowed temples lavishly, and Osorkon II rebuilt at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bubastis">Bubastis</a>. Royal princes held regional commands, so the state became a network of Libyan family fiefs. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takelot-ii">Takelot II</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a> rebelled against Prince Osorkon, as his chronicle at Karnak records.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>From about 837 BCE rival kings appeared, including the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/twenty-third-dynasty-of-egypt">Twenty-third Dynasty of Egypt</a>, and the realm fragmented. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piye">Piye's</a> invasion around 728 BCE reduced the dynasty to a minor Delta kingship, and its last kings disappeared under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kushite-empire">Kushite Empire</a> around 720 BCE.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/twenty-second-dynasty-of-egypt.jpg" alt="Twenty-second Dynasty of Egypt" width="320" height="434"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Egypte_louvre_066.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>943 BCE – 720 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century-bce">10th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bubastis</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sheshonq I, Osorkon I, Osorkon II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Egyptian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Egyptian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/egypt">Egypt</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bubastite Dynasty, Libyan Dynasty, Twenty-second Dynasty</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-832&amp;focus=twenty-second-dynasty-of-egypt" aria-label="Twenty-second Dynasty of Egypt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5497 1062 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Twenty-second Dynasty of Egypt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5817 1318L5825 1304M5817 1318L5863 1488M5817 1318L5862 1746M5817 1318L5863 1488"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5825 1304h0M5863 1488h0M5862 1746h0M5863 1488h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5817 1318h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5817 1318h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bubastis. <a href="/atlas?year=-832&amp;focus=twenty-second-dynasty-of-egypt">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
